    "text": {
     "en": "Early humans were hunter-gatherers. They moved about to hunt animals and gather fruits and roots, used stone tools and discovered fire.\nAbout ten thousand years ago people began farming and keeping animals. They settled in villages, grew wheat, barley and rice, and made pots.\nFarming meant more food, so people could build homes, make tools and start trade."
